{"kind":"finding","id":"F-recording-tree-044-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/EffectiveLeafFinalizationTests.cs","line":517,"method":"FinalizeIndividualRecording_MultipleDifferentPidChildren_TreatsParentAsEffectiveLeaf","category":"T3","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/GhostPlaybackLogic.cs:8533-8541; narrowing the child scan to bp.ChildRecordingIds[0] stays green because debris pids 2000/3000 both differ from parent pid 1000, so any single-child check returns true; removing the same-PID child scan -> red on the terminal=Landed and leaf=True asserts","what_it_asserts":"A parent recording with ChildBranchPointId whose branch point holds two different-PID children (debris pids 2000/3000 vs parent 1000) is still the effective leaf for its own PID: FinalizeIndividualRecording stamps terminal Landed and logs leaf=True.","why_weak":"The comment claims the cell pins that the same-PID check considers EVERY child, but with every child PID differing from the parent the verdict is identical under a first-child-only or last-child-only scan, so the every-child property is unwitnessed. The discriminating shape is a non-first child sharing the parent PID.","proposed_action":"Add the mirror case: BP children ordered [different-PID debris, same-PID continuation]; assert the parent is NOT an effective leaf (TerminalStateValue stays unset, log leaf=False). Or delete the every-child sentence from the comment.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"coverage","sut":"GhostPlaybackLogic","sut_file":"Source/Parsek/GhostPlaybackLogic.cs","sut_line":8533,"case_kind":"mirror-direction","proposed_name":"IsEffectiveLeafForVessel_SamePidChildNotFirst_ReturnsFalse","sketch":"Recording parent (pid 1000, ChildBranchPointId bp) with treeContext; bp.ChildRecordingIds = [debris pid 2000, continuation pid 1000]; assert IsEffectiveLeafForVessel(parent, tree) false, and a variant with both children differing assert true. A first-child-only scan returns true for the mirror shape.","guards":"The every-child same-PID scan at GhostPlaybackLogic.cs:8533-8541; the committed cell at EffectiveLeafFinalizationTests.cs:517 uses two different-PID children, so a narrowed scan stays green.","risk":"recording"}
